  "goodToKnow": "Der Stadtkern is the town centre or core: der historische Stadtkern, often a medieval Altstadt with half-timbered houses. Many German towns struggle with empty shops there (Innenstadtsterben) as shopping moves online. Der Kern means core, kernel or fruit stone. Synonyms: die Innenstadt, das Zentrum. The opposite is der Stadtrand (outskirts). Plural: die Stadtkerne."
